#!/bin/bash
# tests/e2e/stubs/ssh-keygen — deterministic keys. The fragments only need key
# files to exist with stable content (they are catted, base64'd and chmodded);
# real key generation would be slower and non-deterministic.
STATE="${E2E_STATE:?E2E_STATE not set}"
f=""
prev=""
for a in "$@"; do
  if [ "$prev" = "-f" ]; then f="$a"; prev=""; continue; fi
  case "$a" in
    -f) prev="-f" ;;
  esac
done
[ -n "$f" ] || { echo "e2e ssh-keygen stub: no -f path in: $*" >&2; exit 1; }
base="$(basename "$f")"
printf 'E2E-PRIVATE-KEY-FOR-%s\n' "$base" > "$f"
printf 'ssh-ed25519 E2EPUB-%s e2e@test\n' "$base" > "$f.pub"
printf 'ssh-keygen %s\n' "$*" >> "$STATE/journal"
exit 0
